Mark 15:1 , Jesus brought bound, and accused before Pilate;
Mark 15:6 , Upon the clamour of the common people, the murderer Barabbas is loosed, and Jesus delivered up to be crucified;
Mark 15:16 , He is crowned with thorns, spit on, and mocked;
Mark 15:21 , faints in bearing his cross;
Mark 15:27 , hangs between two thieves;
Mark 15:29 , suffers the triumphing reproaches of the Jews;
Mark 15:39 , but is confessed by the centurion to be the Son of God;
Mark 15:42 , and is honourably buried by Joseph.
